From 17016efd143c4312a39719da6a526a9909f7a53c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:42:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MERGE-0b3a0735: laptop packages 102-104 (GitHub main 309a6d3,
 GitLab main 0b3a0735) into the machine tree

Package 102 (GitLab 5ae25f4d): per golden the safe-door locks follow the run state (locked while running, released after
stop; the Magazine doors too -- IO moves), the big fan follows the FAN button, TfMain::SetLotState sends LOTNUMBER /
LOTSTART / LOTEND to a TCP/IP tester and the lot state to the GPIB bridge.
Package 103 (GitLab 7ea471cf): docs only.
Package 104 (GitLab 0b3a0735): per golden fMain->Pause really pauses the machine again (~40 state-machine sites,
RemoteControl / RCMD:PAUSE), SECS REMOTE_START reaches the HTSET,333 seat, [I06] writes config.ini after home, Jerry's
CheckSocketSensor per golden.

20 files: NEW 7, OLD 13 (machine had an older laptop version, taken as is), LOCAL 0 -- nothing changed on both sides.
No file under tools/vscode-htdesigner. o2: wb_serve + 7 tests build, PE 28/28 (o2) and 178/178 (the F5 build, built
from these same sources at 13:26) complete; ctest MainTimerSegments / PauseForward / SetLotState / SocketSensor /
VacuumVc8 / MachineIoTable_HT9050 / IoPoints_HT9050 / MachineSuckers_HT9050 pass. WebMotorAccess and TempFuseLimit
were NOT run here: Windows refused to start their exes ("Access is denied", ctest "operation not permitted") -- the
files read fine and their ACLs are normal; Trend Micro's behaviour monitor is the likely cause. Their sources are not
in these packages (both passed in the 100-101 round). production_audit unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
